k{flex-wrap:wrap}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-central-cell{flex:0 0 100%;order:-2;width:auto}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-back,.mw-parser-output .wst-header-forward{width:auto}}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-notes{display:inline-block;border-collapse:collapse;border-spacing:0;empty-cells:hide;font-size:.9em;line-height:1.4;margin:0 auto 4px auto;width:100%}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-left{float:left}</style><div class=\"ws-header wst-header-structure wst-unknown wst-header ws-header ws-noexport noprint dynlayout-exempt\"><div class=\"wst-header-mainblock wst-unknown-mainblock headertemplate\"><div class=\"wst-header-back searchaux wst-unknown-back\"><div class=\"wst-header-back-arrow\">\u2190</div><div class=\"wst-header-back-link\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Army_and_Navy_Hymnal/Hymns/A_Mighty_Fortress_is_Our_God\" title=\"The Army and Navy Hymnal/Hymns/A Mighty Fortress is Our God\">A Mighty Fortress is Our God</a></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-central-cell wst-unknown-central-cell\"><span class=\"wst-header-title wst-unknown-title\"><span class=\"wst-header-title-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Army_and_Navy_Hymnal\" title=\"The Army and Navy Hymnal\">The Army and Navy Hymnal</a></span><br class=\"wst-header-title-break\" /><span class=\"contributor-text\">edited by&#160;<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Author:Henry_Augustine_Smith\" title=\"Author:Henry Augustine Smith\">Henry Augustine Smith</a></span></span><div class=\"header-section-text\">How Firm a Foundation <span class=\"contributor-text\">by&#160;<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Portal:Anonymous_texts\" title=\"Portal:Anonymous texts\">Anonymous</a></span></span></div></span></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward searchaux wst-unknown-forward\"><div class=\"wst-header-forward-link\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Army_and_Navy_Hymnal/Hymns/Forward!_Be_Our_Watchword\" title=\"The Army and Navy Hymnal/Hymns/Forward! Be Our Watchword\">Forward! Be Our Watchword</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><div class=\"wst-header-content header&#95;notes&#95;content wst-header-notes-content wst-unknown-notes-content\">\n<p>The hymn \"<b>How Firm a Foundation</b>\" first appeared in <a href=\"/wiki/Author:John_Rippon\" title=\"Author:John Rippon\">John Rippon</a>'s <i><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=A_Selection_of_Hymns&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"A Selection of Hymns (page does not exist)\">A Selection of Hymns</a></i> (1787), where it was attributed simply to \"K\". The most likely candidates for \"K\" are <a href=\"/wiki/Author:Robert_Keene\" title=\"Author:Robert Keene\">Robert Keene</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Author:George_Keith\" title=\"Author:George Keith\">George Keith</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Author:Thomas_Kirkham\" title=\"Author:Thomas Kirkham\">Thomas Kirkham</a>, or someone named \"Kennedy\".\n</p><p>The anonymous tune is that used for \"<a href=\"/wiki/Adeste_Fideles\" class=\"mw-disambig\" title=\"Adeste Fideles\">Adeste Fideles</a>\". The earliest known version comes from <i><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=Cantus_Diversi&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Cantus Diversi (page does not exist)\">Cantus Diversi</a></i> by <a href=\"/wiki/Author:John_Francis_Wade\" title=\"Author:John Francis Wade\">John Francis Wade</a>, but has also been attributed to <a href=\"/wiki/Author:John_Reading\" title=\"Author:John Reading\">John Reading</a> or King <a href=\"/wiki/Author:John_IV_of_Portugal\" title=\"Author:John IV of Portugal\">John IV of Portugal</a>\n</p>\n</div></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">1868226</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Army_and_Navy_Hymnal\" title=\"The Army and Navy Hymnal\">The Army and Navy Hymnal</a> \u2014 How Firm a Foundation</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Henry Augustine Smith</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Anonymous</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r12314949/mw-parser-output/.prp-pages-output\">.mw-parser-output .prp-pages-output .ws-poem-versenum:after,.mw-parser-output .prp-pages-output .verse_num:after{content:\".\";padding-right:0.25em}.mw-parser-output .prp-pages-output .ps2-character{font-variant:small-caps;text-align:left}</style><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"106\" data-page-number=\"106\" data-page-name=\"Page:The Army and Navy Hymnal.djvu/137\" data-page-index=\"137\" data-page-quality=\"2\" title=\"Page:The&#95;Army&#95;and&#95;Navy&#95;Hymnal.djvu/137\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;137\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15620827\">.mw-parser-output .wst-center{text-align:center;margin:0 auto}.mw-parser-output .wst-center.wst-center-nomargin>p{margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0}</style><div class=\"wst-center tiInherit\">\n<div class=\"mw-ext-score-disabled\">Musical scores are temporarily disabled.</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"poem\">\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431465\">.mw-parser-output .wst-block-center{display:block;margin:0 auto;padding:0;position:relative;max-width:100%;height:auto;text-align:initial}.mw-parser-output .wst-block-center-title{display:inline-block;width:100%;text-align:center}</style><div class=\"wst-block-center\" style=\"width:fit-content;\">\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15551948\">.mw-parser-output .wst_list_continuation>li:first-child{list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none}.mw-parser-output .wst_ulist.__idx_hi1,.mw-parser-output .wst_ulist.__plain{line-height:inherit;list-style:none;list-style-image:none;margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst_ulist.__nomarker{line-height:inherit;list-style:none;list-style-image:none}.mw-parser-output .__fixleft{margin-left:1.6em}.mw-parser-output .wst_olist.__idx_hi1 ol,.mw-parser-output .wst_olist.__plain ol,.mw-parser-output .wst_ulist.__idx_hi1 ul,.mw-parser-output .wst_ulist.__plain ul{margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0}.mw-parser-output .wst_olist.__plain li,.mw-parser-output .wst_ulist.__plain li{margin-bottom:0}.mw-parser-output .wst_olist.__idx_hi1 li,.mw-parser-output .wst_ulist.__idx_hi1 li{margin-left:1em;text-indent:-1em;margin-bottom:0}.mw-parser-output .wst_list_continuation.__idx_hi1>li:first-child{list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;margin-left:1em;text-indent:0}.mw-parser-output .wst_olist.__inside,.mw-parser-output .wst_ulist.__inside{list-style-position:inside;margin-left:0}</style><ol class=\"wst&#95;olist\"><li>How firm a foundation, ye saints of the Lord, <br />\nIs laid for your faith in his excellent word! <br />\nWhat more can he say than to you he hath said, <br />\nTo you  who for refuge to Jesus have fled? <br />\nTo you who for refuge to Jesus have fled? <br /></li><li>'Fear not, I am with thee, O be not dismayed&#160;; <br />\nFor I am thy God, I will still give thee aid: <br />\nI'll strengthen thee, help thee, and cause thee to stand, <br />\nUpheld by my righteous, omnipotent hand, <br />\nUpheld by my righteous, omnipotent hand.<br /></li><li>'When thro' the deep waters I call thee to go, <br />\nThe rivers of sorrow shall not overflow&#160;; <br />\nFor I will be near thee, thy troubles to bless, <br />\nAnd sanctify to thee thy deepest distress, <br />\nAnd sanctify to thee thy deepest distress.<br /></li><li>'The soul that on Jesus hath leaned for repose, <br />\nI will not, I will not desert to his foes; <br />\nThat soul tho' all hell should endeavor to shake, <br />\nI'll nev er, no, never, no never forsake, <br />\nI'll nev er, no, never, no never forsake.<span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Amen</span></li></ol>\n</div>\n</div>&#32;\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw\u2010api\u2010ext.codfw.main\u20108f5c67887\u2010cn55r\nCache